# MCP Tools: githubmcp

ALWAYS include `arguments` in CallMcpTool calls. NEVER send empty `{}`.

### add_pr_comment
Add a comment to a pull request.

| Field | Type | Required | Default | Description |
|-------|------|----------|---------|-------------|
| `owner` | string | yes |  | Repository owner (user or organization). |
| `repo` | string | yes |  | Repository name. |
| `pull_number` | integer | yes |  | The pull request number to comment on. |
| `body` | string | yes |  | Comment text (supports Markdown). |

Example:
CallMcpTool({ server: "githubmcp", toolName: "add_pr_comment", arguments: {"owner": "lqdflying", "repo": "chathub", "pull_number": 5, "body": "Content"} })

### create_branch
Create a new branch in a GitHub repository.

| Field | Type | Required | Default | Description |
|-------|------|----------|---------|-------------|
| `owner` | string | yes |  | Repository owner (user or organization). |
| `repo` | string | yes |  | Repository name. |
| `branch` | string | yes |  | Name of the new branch to create (e.g. "feature/my-feature"). |
| `from_ref` | string \| null | no | `null` | Branch name, tag, or commit SHA to branch off from.<br>      Defaults to the repo's default branch. |

Example:
CallMcpTool({ server: "githubmcp", toolName: "create_branch", arguments: {"owner": "lqdflying", "repo": "chathub", "branch": "main"} })

### create_issue
Create a new issue in a GitHub repository.

| Field | Type | Required | Default | Description |
|-------|------|----------|---------|-------------|
| `owner` | string | yes |  | Repository owner (user or organization). |
| `repo` | string | yes |  | Repository name. |
| `title` | string | yes |  | Issue title. |
| `body` | string | no | `""` | Optional issue body (supports Markdown). |
| `labels` | array<string> \| null | no | `null` | Optional list of label names to apply (e.g. ["bug", "help wanted"]). |

Example:
CallMcpTool({ server: "githubmcp", toolName: "create_issue", arguments: {"owner": "lqdflying", "repo": "chathub", "title": "Title"} })

### create_pull_request
Create a new pull request in a GitHub repository.

| Field | Type | Required | Default | Description |
|-------|------|----------|---------|-------------|
| `owner` | string | yes |  | Repository owner (user or organization). |
| `repo` | string | yes |  | Repository name. |
| `title` | string | yes |  | PR title. |
| `head` | string | yes |  | The branch containing your changes (e.g. "feature/my-feature"). |
| `base` | string | yes |  | The branch you want to merge into (e.g. "main"). |
| `body` | string | no | `""` | Optional PR description (supports Markdown). |
| `draft` | boolean | no | `false` | If True, open as a draft pull request. |

Example:
CallMcpTool({ server: "githubmcp", toolName: "create_pull_request", arguments: {"owner": "lqdflying", "repo": "chathub", "title": "Title", "head": "value", "base": "value"} })

### delete_file
Delete a file from a GitHub repository branch.

| Field | Type | Required | Default | Description |
|-------|------|----------|---------|-------------|
| `owner` | string | yes |  | Repository owner (user or organization). |
| `repo` | string | yes |  | Repository name. |
| `path` | string | yes |  | Path of the file to delete (e.g. "src/old_module.py"). |
| `message` | string | yes |  | Commit message for the deletion. |
| `branch` | string | yes |  | Branch to delete the file from. |

Example:
CallMcpTool({ server: "githubmcp", toolName: "delete_file", arguments: {"owner": "lqdflying", "repo": "chathub", "path": "README.md", "message": "Content", "branch": "main"} })

### find_files
Search for files matching a glob pattern in a GitHub repository.

| Field | Type | Required | Default | Description |
|-------|------|----------|---------|-------------|
| `owner` | string | yes |  | Repository owner (user or organization). |
| `repo` | string | yes |  | Repository name. |
| `pattern` | string | yes |  | Glob pattern to match file paths (e.g. "**/*.py", "src/**/*.ts", "*.md"). |
| `ref` | string \| null | no | `null` | Branch, tag, or commit SHA. Defaults to the repo's default branch. |

Example:
CallMcpTool({ server: "githubmcp", toolName: "find_files", arguments: {"owner": "lqdflying", "repo": "chathub", "pattern": "value"} })

### get_blame
Get blame information for a file, showing which commit last modified each line.

| Field | Type | Required | Default | Description |
|-------|------|----------|---------|-------------|
| `owner` | string | yes |  | Repository owner (user or organization). |
| `repo` | string | yes |  | Repository name. |
| `path` | string | yes |  | File path within the repository. |
| `ref` | string | no | `"HEAD"` | Branch, tag, or commit SHA. Defaults to HEAD. |

Example:
CallMcpTool({ server: "githubmcp", toolName: "get_blame", arguments: {"owner": "lqdflying", "repo": "chathub", "path": "README.md"} })

### get_commits
Get commit history for a repository or specific file.

| Field | Type | Required | Default | Description |
|-------|------|----------|---------|-------------|
| `owner` | string | yes |  | Repository owner (user or organization). |
| `repo` | string | yes |  | Repository name. |
| `ref` | string \| null | no | `null` | Branch, tag, or commit SHA to start from. Defaults to the repo's default branch. |
| `path` | string \| null | no | `null` | Optional file path to filter commits that touched this file. |
| `limit` | integer | no | `20` | Maximum number of commits to return (default: 20). |

Example:
CallMcpTool({ server: "githubmcp", toolName: "get_commits", arguments: {"owner": "lqdflying", "repo": "chathub"} })

